Principle: Single Responsibility

Let's separate the responsibilities into two private helpers:

i2c_wait_sr1_flag()
  Responsible for
    polling
    timeout
    classifying the error
    returning status

        │
        ▼
Read SR1 once
        │
        ├── Success → return OK
        │
        ├── AF?
        │      │
        │      ▼
        │ clear_error_flags(sr1)
        │ return NACK
        │
        ├── BERR?
        │      │
        │      ▼
        │ clear_error_flags(sr1)
        │ return BUS
        │
        └── Timeout

---Detection happens in one place.
---Recovery/Cleanup happens in another.
---Future interrupt and DMA versions can reuse the cleanup function.
================================================================
Let public transaction APIs own recovery

When we implement i2c_write(), the flow will be:

            Validate Parameters
                    ↓
            Check Driver State // free/ready, busy
                    ↓
            Set State = BUSY_TX // assign state, TAKING OWNERSHIP 
                    ↓
            Generate START      // then start the i2c_generate_start
                    ↓
            Send Address (Write) //i2c_send_address
                    ↓
            Loop Through Buffer // dta length
                    ↓
                Send Byte      //i2c_send_byte
                    ↓
            Generate STOP      //i2c_generate_stop
                    ↓
            State = READY      // free state 
                    ↓
            Return Status      // report back to caller func

If any primitive returns an error:

Primitive Error
        ↓
i2c_reset_bus()
        ↓
Return Error

This keeps the layering clean:

