i2c_abort_sequence()
    ├── If still master: request STOP
    ├── If not master: cancel pending START
    └── Preserve and return the original error
_______________________________________
Because the improved i2c_init() now resets the peripheral through:

RCC->APB1RSTR |= RCC_APB1RSTR_I2C1RST;
RCC->APB1RSTR &= ~RCC_APB1RSTR_I2C1RST;

that performs an actual hardware reset before returning the driver to READY.
State contract:

READY
  ↓ transaction failure
ERROR
  ↓ i2c_init()
RESET hardware → configure → READY
Later, when implementing the interrupt/DMA version, a dedicated public recovery API may be justified:

i2c_status_t i2c_recover(void);
But that function must recover and validate the hardware, not merely modify s_state.
